Package: xlamisc
Title: Tensor Generics and Data Types for the 'XLA' Ecosystem
Version: 0.4.1.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sebastian", "Fischer", , "seb.fischer@tutamail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9609-3197")),
    person("Daniel", "Falbel", , "daniel@posit.co", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0143-2392"))
  )
Description: Provides S3 generics for querying tensors, such as their shape,
    data type and device, and for converting them to R arrays and raw
    vectors. Also provides an enum-style class for tensor element types
    (booleans, signed and unsigned integers, floats and complex numbers)
    together with helpers to inspect their category and bit width. These
    are shared by the packages that bring 'XLA' <https://openxla.org/xla>
    to R.
